We introduce the NiPura Directed Dynamical Systems (NDDS) framework, establishing a geometric unification of 3D Navier-Stokes regularity, Yang-Mills mass gap, and QCD confinement via an azimuthal principal bundle. We prove that strict positivity of directional coherence $S\_{\\rm Ni}(t) &gt; \\delta &gt; 0$ induces geometric depletion of vortex stretching (modified Beale-Kato-Majda bound). The same mechanism quantizes the Chern-Simons invariant to multiples of 1/94, generating the mass gap and explaining permanent quark confinement. The framework is holographically realized in AdS/CFT, yielding testable predictions for glueball spectra and string tension. Numerical and holographic evidence is provided.
