\noindent\textbf{Keywords:} Navier-Stokes regularity, azimuthal fibrations, Chern-Simons invariant, Yang-Mills mass gap, QCD confinement, AdS/CFT holography.
\section{Introduction}
The global regularity of 3D Navier-Stokes and the mass gap of Yang-Mills are two of the seven Millennium Prize Problems. We propose a unified geometric solution based on a single object: the **fibré d’Azimut**.
The master equation of the framework is
\begin{equation}
P_{\rm taxi}(t) + X \cdot h(t) \cdot E(t)^2 \cdot \xi(t) = \Omega(t).
